WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.820
Stage zero matters because the
target has to reproduce intent,

2
00:00:03.820 --> 00:00:07.300
not structure, and you can't
reproduce what you haven't read.

3
00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:09.038
It's entirely read-only.

4
00:00:09.038 --> 00:00:12.245
Capture each O U's placement,
its Group Policy links,

5
00:00:12.245 --> 00:00:15.987
and especially the permissions
someone delegated by hand.

6
00:00:15.987 --> 00:00:20.682
Then decide every group's fate, and
split the Group Policy settings by track:

7
00:00:20.682 --> 00:00:25.300
user settings go with people, computer
settings with devices and servers.

8
00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:29.843
Two traps: a policy linked at a site
looks unlinked if you only search O U's,

9
00:00:29.843 --> 00:00:33.462
and the protected-account
marker overstates privilege.

10
00:00:33.462 --> 00:00:34.920
Now the attributes.
